    check="A 5 TB drive shows as roughly 4.5 TB in Windows, because Windows counts in binary units. That’s normal. A partition that reports far more space than the drive holds is not normal, and it’s a sign of a damaged partition table. Stop writing to the drive and see the troubleshooting guides below."
    facts="Model WDBU6Y0050BBK-WESN, 5 TB. The Amazon listing describes it as USB 3.2 Gen 1/USB 3.0, for PC and Mac. Confirm current specifications and warranty terms with Western Digital."
